Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('4f6c375e15c9bb5569bd7856e2ef36bdf601cc537a2cfab816b032103a2665f3',), event=Revised(decision='lensplanning', at=datetime(2026, 11, 6, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='Plan a change as a named expert would have written it, then review it through the same eyes', body='Every brief names the people whose work the change should read like. The standing roster: Alexis King (make invalid states unrepresentable; parse, do not validate), Justin Le (types and functor combinators that compose), Edward Kmett (one general combinator with laws), Evan Czaplicki (the Elm architecture: one model, one update, a view of values), the Rust maintainers (idiom and API), and the git and Pijul maintainers (stores and history). Before writing code, the agent asks how they would have shaped this change: which types, which one general piece, what they would delete. It plans the change around that answer and says it in the pull request. After writing, it reviews the result through the same eyes. A lens that only reviews finds problems too late to change the design.', rationale='The owner, 2026-11-06: an agent should ask itself whether this is how that person would have written the code, and plan the changes around how they would have written it, when making new changes; the owner added Justin Le and Alexis King to the names.', supersedes=()))